FILE-18: round rule premise times to whole seconds

newpremise() stored a SYSTEM TIME or CLOCKTIME premise as hour() * 3600,
which is not a whole number for many clock times: 8:00:01 becomes
28800.999999999996 s. checktime() truncates it to 28800 s, so the rule
can fire a rule step early, and gettimetxt() writes it back as 8:00:00.
The time is now rounded to the nearest second, as timedata() does for
[TIMES] and the FILE-05 fix does for [CONTROLS].

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply FILE-18_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/rules.c b/src/rules.c
index 1b009ad..8b43849 100644
--- a/src/rules.c
+++ b/src/rules.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <string.h>
+#include <math.h>
 
 #include "types.h"
 #include "funcs.h"
@@ -824,6 +825,7 @@ int newpremise(Project *pr, int logop)
         if (parser->Ntokens == 6) x = hour(Tok[4], Tok[5]) * 3600.;
         else                      x = hour(Tok[4], "") * 3600.;
         if (x < 0.0) return 202;
+        x = floor(x + 0.5);  // whole seconds, e.g. 8:00:01 is 28800.999...
